    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1040">

                <pb facs="1333" n="1323" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg1323"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.003/3–1546</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Smyth</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-03-15T14:00:00+07:00">March 15, 1946—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 21—1:37 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>494. Purpose of Embtel 330, February 20, 8 a.m. (Reurtel 401, March 5) was to
                    enable us to answer inquiry made by Josselyn at Shanghai in his despatch No. 61
                        [<hi rendition="#italic">21</hi>], February 9,<anchor n="17"
                        xml:id="d1040-f1"/> reconstruction of article 4 of 1943 extraterritoriality
                    treaty. Copy of Josselyn’s despatch has been forwarded to Dept by Shanghai. Copy
                    of our reply to Josselyn being sent by air mail.<anchor n="18" xml:id="d1040-f2"
                    />
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smyth</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
